Description: Admit V4L2 stateless (Request API) decoders in the RDD sandbox
 Stateless V4L2 decoders, used through VA-API by libva-v4l2-request, need the
 media controller device that owns the decoder's video node (request
 allocation) besides the M2M video node the RDD broker already admits. The
 broker adds a /dev/media* node only when its topology exposes one of the
 admitted M2M video nodes, plus that node's sysfs uevent (read-only), so
 webcam and capture media devices stay blocked. The seccomp policy of the RDD
 process allows only MEDIA_IOC_G_TOPOLOGY, MEDIA_IOC_REQUEST_ALLOC and
 MEDIA_REQUEST_IOC_QUEUE/REINIT; MEDIA_IOC_SETUP_LINK and the entity and link
 enumeration stay blocked. Without it Firefox falls back to software decoding
 ("Failed to create VA-API device context") unless MOZ_DISABLE_RDD_SANDBOX=1.
 Backport to 153 ESR of attachments 9682335 (Christian Bartels) and 9686785
 (Arun Iyengar) from the bug, combined; the code is unchanged.
